platform and Hadoop ecosystem.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.950
So I'm finding
three main reasons

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:01.562
why customers are building
data lakes on Google Cloud.

00:01:01.562 --> 00:01:03.520
First of all, there's
just a lot of new sources

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.310
of data coming in from a
variety of places, streaming

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.490
applications, IoT, device data.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:12.130
And that just means there's
a lot more unstructured data

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.960
around that you have to
deal with, secure, analyze.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:22.000
The second reason is that folks
are building data lakes on GCP

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.440
is that just data is becoming
a lot more self-service now.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.480
IT departments,
they're getting away

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.320
from this idea of having a
centralized reporting team.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.540
And I think there's a
lot of reasons for that.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.350
But the primary one is
simply that data now

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.630
is just becoming
way too important

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.190
to wait on all
the inefficiencies

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:45.460
that are typically imposed
by teams like that.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.190
Also the tools for
working with data,

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.590
they're becoming a lot
more mainstream and easier

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:51.740
to work with.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.770
So you're also
finding business users

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:56.530
are a lot more data savvy.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:00.670
And the third reason is
that users now need access

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:03.100
to a lot more data
than they used to,

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.530
a lot more ranges of data.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:09.070
At the same time, businesses
are getting a lot more stringent

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:10.780
privacy regulations.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.560
And they want to protect
their PII trade secrets.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.270
And so companies,
they need to start

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:19.390
automating a lot of those
privacy checks and data access

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:21.050
because you just
can't keep up with all

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:22.870
of the different sources.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.080
Most of the talks focused
today that we're about to do

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.750
is on this third reason.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.530
But we also find that to
satisfy the first two reasons,

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.710
oftentimes, this
is a requirement,

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:38.310
to help with number one and two.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.040
So customers are using
Google Cloud Platform

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.990
to build data lakes
because we have

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:47.130
a lot of those tools that are
commonly found in data lakes.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.860
So whether it's data
ingestion, data processing,

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.350
data management,
or data security,

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:56.350
GCP probably has an
option for your use case.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.655
Now I can't even begin to
