00:02:58.655 --> 00:03:00.780
the different offerings
that you see on this slide,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.100
in this talk.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.530
But what I am going
to try to do is

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.580
I'm going to try to answer for
why security-minded customers,

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:14.440
like yourself, are choosing
GCP to secure their data lakes.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.870
So the GCP platform,
as a whole, we

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:20.810
have independent verification
of our security, privacy,

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.780
and compliance controls.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.240
Google undergoes independent
third-party audits

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.610
on a regular basis to
provide this assurance.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:31.090
So this means that an
independent auditor has come in

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:34.010
and examined all of our controls
and all of our data centers

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:37.660
in our infrastructure
and in our operations.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.130
And so the
certifications that we

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.650
tend to go after, these are
going to be the most widely

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:45.760
recognized, independent,
and widely accepted

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.120
security standards.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.230
So you're going to find things
like ISO for our security

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.873
controls, and cloud
security, and privacy.

00:03:52.873 --> 00:03:54.790
But then we also-- you're
going to find things

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.650
like our SOC 1, 2, and 3.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.530
And all of these certifications,
having these in place,

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.920
what this really helps us do
is meet industry standards

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.640
like PCI, or like HIPAA.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.220
And we're going to continue
to expand the list that you

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.250
see here with
certifications globally

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.800
to make sure that we can
help our customers meet

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.130
their compliance obligations.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.579
Now another reason why
security-minded customers

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:25.140
choose GCP is because we have
deep and wide features that

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:28.090
make it easy to keep
your data secure.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:31.810
So we have default
at-rest encryption.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:34.300
If anyone here has ever had
to deal with doing like a LUKS

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.680
encryption on drives,
you know the pain

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.040
both from a performance and
management perspective--

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.090
like aspects of doing that.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.770
And so Google Cloud, anytime we
land data, it gets encrypted.

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:50.630
And that just makes it easy.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:54.867
But at the same time, you
can often control the keys.

00:04:54.867 --> 00:04:56.950
So if you want to have
customer-managed encryption

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.500
keys for that data that's
stored, you can do that.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.780
You can rotate those
keys on your schedule,

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.660
revoke those keys
as you need to.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.870
Most of our products also
integrate with Stackdriver.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.000
That's going to offer you
